 ("re_bbtu and types", "In Oct 2023 EIA changed how SEDS counts wind, solar, hydro and geothermal (captured energy, 3,412 Btu/kWh; www.eia.gov/state/seds/seds-change/index.php). k = 2.3-2.9 in the old-basis rebuild is our approximation, not EIA's.", "Fang names no SEDS release, but says EIA's data ended in 2021 (PDF p. 3), and its Table 2 constants imply a mean log outcome of about 11.79, which fits the old basis and not the current one (11.44). The change explains the sign difference with Fang, not the full size.", "Data"),
 ("Net producer", "Our rule is EIA generation above retail sales on each state's 2018-2021 average: 120 state-years, against Fang's 76 (rule at PDF p. 4; series not stated). SEDS total energy production above consumption gives 40; SEDS net interstate electricity flow below zero gives 104.", "None reaches 76, so we can't confirm Fang's groups. The gap between groups in Fang's spec is significant on our rule only. Exploratory.", "Data"),
 ("co2_power_t, co2_per_mwh_t", "CO2 ends in 2024.", "2025 is blank; Step 4 CO2 rows stop at 2024.", "Data"),
 ("price_c_kwh", "Average revenue per kWh, all sectors.", "Not a marginal price, and it moves with sector mix.", "Data"),
